  "comment": "Policy 42. Vivaldi and Ecosia join Chrome and Firefox Focus on the allowed browser list, so there is a choice rather than a single imposed browser. All four are Chromium or Gecko builds with no proxy of their own; Firefox stays out because it offers a VPN, and Opera and the other proxy browsers are blocked by name in policy 41. herald remains allowed_browser_package, which as of drawbridge 0.2.8 build 23 is finally read: the DPC makes it the persistent handler for web links, so a tapped link opens in herald while the others stay available to whoever launches them. That preference is set by a Device Owner API and cannot be changed in Settings.",
